  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) R.C. 3509.06(D)(3)(b)\n(quote) If the election officials find that the identification envelope statement of voter is incomplete or that the information contained in that statement does not conform to the information contained in the statewide voter registration database concerning the voter, the election officials shall mail a written notice to the voter, informing the voter of the nature of the defect. The notice shall inform the voter that in order for the voter's ballot to be counted, the voter must provide the necessary information to the board of elections in writing and on a form prescribed by the secretary of state not later than the seventh day after the day of the election.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) R.C. 3509.03(E)\n(quote) One of the following: (1) The elector's driver's license number; (2) The last four digits of the elector's social security number; (3) A copy of the elector's current and valid photo identification, a copy of a military identification, or a copy of a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document, other than a notice of voter registration mailed by a board of elections under section 3503.19 of the Revised Code, that shows the name and address of the elector.\n(section) R.C. 3509.06(D)(3)(a)(v)\n(quote) One of the following forms of identification: (I) The voter's driver's license number; (II) The last four digits of the voter's social security number; or (III) A copy of a current and valid photo identification, a military identification, or a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document, other than a notice of voter registration mailed by a board of elections, that shows the voter's name and address.\n(section) R.C. 3509.04, 3509.03 (new)\n(quote) A board of elections may preprint only an elector's name and address on an identification envelope statement of voter before mailing absent voter's ballots to the elector.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) R.C. 3509.06(D)(3)(a)\n(quote) An identification envelope statement of voter shall be considered incomplete if it does not include all of the following: (i) The voter's name; (ii) The voter's residence address; (iii) The voter's date of birth.\n(other) R.C. 3501.05, 3505.24: Secretary of State and board duties; assistance in marking ballots (conforming)\n(other) R.C. 3509.03 / 3509.04: only name and address may be preprinted on absentee applications and envelope statements; the elector must fill out the rest\n(other) R.C. 3509.06: what makes an envelope statement incomplete; board must mail notice of the defect; voter may fix by the seventh day after the election\n(other) R.C. 3509.07: list of grounds on which an absentee ballot is not counted, with the seventh-day fix exception\n(other) R.C. 3511.02, 3511.04, 3511.05, 3511.10: same preprint limits and responsibilities for uniformed and overseas absentee voters\n(other) version: 00_IN: absentee ID options (DL number, SSN-4, or copy of photo ID / utility bill etc.) in 3509.03 and the envelope statement; no cure text\n(other) version: 01_RS: adds the limit on preprinting by officials; same absentee ID text\n(other) version: 02_PS: same as 01_RS\n(other) version: 03_RH: adds the seventh-day cure for an incomplete or non-matching envelope statement\n(other) version: 04_PH: same as 03_RH\n(other) version: 05_EN: same ID text and seventh-day cure as 03_RH; no in-person ID, no citizenship proof\n(other) note: 2014 PDF text. Struck and new words are not marked; the absentee ID options are reprinted existing law (the bill's title is about mailing and who completes ballot documents), so I cannot tell if any ID wording is new. New text I could detect by comparing versions: the preprint limit (from 01_RS), the 'incomplete' definition and the seventh-day cure (from 03_RH). Vote mapping per brief: Senate passage on 01_RS, House passage on 03_RH, Senate concurrence on 04_PH; the three House 'laid on table' votes are on floor amendments whose text I do not have.",
